WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:00.950
Hi, everybody.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.901
Let's talk about digital employees, or digeys.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.572
I'm Leslie Chau with IBM Automation.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.189
What is a digital employee?

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.692
What can it do for you?

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.880
And what value does it bring to the human workforce?

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.077
Let's start by looking at an example.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.997
I'd like you to meet Cassie.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.615
Cassie is a recruiter.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.906
She helps people like Ava.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.102
Ava is a manager.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.592
And Ava's looking to hire for her team.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.139
Cassie helps Ava with the end-to-end hiring process.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.319
Among other things that she does, she helps Ava look for candidates for her job.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.780
Her typical workflow looks something like this.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:01:00.228
She starts by using LinkedIn recruiter to search for and find the right candidates for the job.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:09.570
She then goes through the search results and finds matching candidates that are qualified for the job.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:16.306
She then messages these candidates and schedules a screening interview

00:01:16.306 --> 00:01:19.728
to make sure that they are the right match for Ava.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:24.164
And then finally, when she has the right list of short-listed candidates,

00:01:24.164 --> 00:01:27.469
she compiles that list into a spreadsheet

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:32.291
so that Ava can then proceed to the next step.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:40.100
Now, Cassie. She wants to spend more of her time doing this.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:49.196
These are higher value tasks, like reviewing resumes or thoughtfully preparing for the screening interview

00:01:49.196 --> 00:01:53.486
so that she can have a best set of candidates for Ava.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.740
She also knows that as a recruiter, this is where she can really flex her skills.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:05.231
But instead, she spends most of her day on manual and repetitive tasks.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:12.352
These are things like combing through a list of candidates in the search results.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.736
Later in the process, when she's come up with the shortlist of candidates,

00:02:19.736 --> 00:02:23.092
she spends a lot of her time copy/pasting.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.689
She copy/pastes information from LinkedIn into the spreadsheet

00:02:28.689 --> 00:02:31.311
to prepare that for Ava to review.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.478
She also spends a lot of her time in administrative tasks like messaging Ava,

00:02:36.478 --> 00:02:39.711
messaging the candidates, scheduling time with the candidates.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:43.691
Now, wouldn't it be great if Cassie had her own personal helper

00:02:43.691 --> 00:02:45.939
that can help her do these manual tasks?

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.372
So that she can focus on some of these more higher value tasks

00:02:50.372 --> 00:02:56.226
that really require, you know, the human skills and the intuition and the analytics.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.121
This is where the digital employee comes in.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.460
I'd like you to meet HenRy.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:09.462
Henry as an HR digital employee and Cassie's new sidekick.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.554
The digital employees have three main functions.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.900
First, it can interact with the world around it.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.039
It can interact with Cassie.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:26.428
Second, it has AI and it can interpret what is being asked to do.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:30.399
And finally it can do work.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:37.322
But just like human employees, digital employees have a set of job skills.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.927
For digital employees,

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:48.637
these are essentially API calls and software robotics.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:00.719
These skills help the digital employee interact with systems

00:04:00.719 --> 00:04:05.560
such as LinkedIn and spreadsheets on behalf of Cassie.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:09.821
So that all Cassi has to do is ask.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:16.331
Cassie asks HenRy to do something

00:04:16.331 --> 00:04:20.853
and HenRy, in turn, uses his AI to interpret what that ask is

00:04:20.853 --> 00:04:26.414
and then match it to the skills that it has to do the work for Cassie.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:33.100
In this example, Cassie can simply ask HenRy to do the search for the candidates in LinkedIn.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:39.069
Now HenRy can interpret that and quickly match it to the LinkedIn skill that it has.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.140
So it will call the LinkedIn API to do the search.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.305
It can even go one step further and message the right candidates

00:04:48.305 --> 00:04:53.290
and schedule a time for Cassie to have the screening interviews with the candidates.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:05:03.355
Later on the process, Cassie can ask HenRy to take the short-listed candidates and compiled them into lists in the spreadsheet.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:09.126
HenRy will interpret that and match it to its spreadsheet skill.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:16.000
It will manually copy/paste each and every row of the short lists into the spreadsheet

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.546
and can even go and signal to Ava when that list is ready for her to review.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:34.377
This was a very simple example, but it shows you how a digital employee can help Cassie save hours of time of manual work.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:39.343
Now Cassie can focus some more of her attention on higher value work

00:05:39.343 --> 00:05:43.957
and where she can spend more of her time now reviewing resumes

00:05:43.957 --> 00:05:49.994
and thoughtfully preparing for those interviews so that she can come up with a better list of candidates for Ava.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:55.224
She can even start differentiating herself now from her peers

00:05:55.224 --> 00:06:02.414
by writing thoughtful recommendations to Ava so Ava can make a better decision and the next steps.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.779
This was a quick overview of digital employees.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.923
If you would like to learn more about digital employees such as how you actually build one,

00:06:11.923 --> 00:06:14.499
be sure to smash that "Subscribe" button.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:19.270
If you liked the video or have a question or comment,

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.799
be sure to hit that "Like" button and leave your comment in the comments section.

